WEBVTT

00:01:32.840 --> 00:01:36.500
<i>"Not a single human</i>
<i>remains on that blue world."</i>

00:01:37.210 --> 00:01:39.570
<i>"How unnatural that is,"</i>
<i>I thought.</i>

00:01:40.640 --> 00:01:43.010
<i>Everything began from there.</i>

00:01:43.880 --> 00:01:45.540
That's correct.

00:01:53.360 --> 00:01:55.050
G-Phaetus!

00:01:55.990 --> 00:01:59.100
There, within accelerated time,

00:01:59.100 --> 00:02:02.120
the meta-bodies continue to
unceasingly evolve and transfigure.

00:02:02.930 --> 00:02:05.560
They no longer have a goal or a reason.

00:02:08.910 --> 00:02:12.470
All they have left is an obsession to evolve.

00:02:14.280 --> 00:02:16.680
Just what is "life"?

00:02:16.680 --> 00:02:20.120
Aren't "people" simply vessels for
the transport of genetic material?

00:02:21.750 --> 00:02:25.480
Go now. Follow the path you believe in.

00:02:25.690 --> 00:02:26.920
However...

00:02:27.620 --> 00:02:29.560
Time is not infinite.

00:02:51.550 --> 00:02:54.480
I've been dreaming a lot lately.

00:02:54.990 --> 00:02:56.610
I envy you.

00:02:58.050 --> 00:03:00.020
I've never had a dream.

00:03:02.190 --> 00:03:05.360
The two of us live with
such sad destinies, don't we?

00:03:11.900 --> 00:03:13.430
Commander Shima.

00:03:16.340 --> 00:03:18.240
It looks like you're all here.

00:03:18.580 --> 00:03:21.680
What's the idea calling us out
here first thing in the morning?

00:03:21.680 --> 00:03:23.670
Gonna have us do radio calisthenics?

00:03:24.380 --> 00:03:27.220
At dawn today,
we finished analyzing the data...

00:03:27.220 --> 00:03:30.580
collected from the Anti-Zega
during the last operation.

00:03:31.090 --> 00:03:35.320
We've confirmed everything we need to know
about the Gards-orm's Arctic core server.

00:03:36.190 --> 00:03:38.400
While it's currently idling,

00:03:38.400 --> 00:03:41.300
we can guess from
the huge energy levels...

00:03:41.300 --> 00:03:45.170
that it may affect every
deutera zone across the Earth.

00:03:45.740 --> 00:03:48.270
Based on all the available facts,

00:03:48.270 --> 00:03:51.710
the commander has a...
vital... announcement to make.

00:03:52.810 --> 00:03:54.680
We'll start with my conclusion.

00:03:54.680 --> 00:03:57.740
The time has come to
initiate the final operation.

00:03:59.480 --> 00:04:01.250
Final operation?

00:04:01.250 --> 00:04:05.760
Concentrate all of humanity's military
might and hit the Arctic core server.

00:04:05.760 --> 00:04:10.060
Eliminate the threat, and then
use their quantum portal.

00:04:11.290 --> 00:04:13.060
We're going to the moon.

00:04:13.400 --> 00:04:14.460
To the moon?!

00:04:14.460 --> 00:04:16.560
What's brought this on?!

00:04:17.170 --> 00:04:19.540
This is the chance
we've been waiting for.

00:04:19.540 --> 00:04:23.400
If we go to the moon, we realize the
dream we've had for so many years.

00:04:24.040 --> 00:04:29.540
Mankind can become physical life forms
once more and be reborn into the real world!

00:04:31.780 --> 00:04:34.750
Reborn into the real world?!

00:04:35.550 --> 00:04:39.780
It is for this day that we've been collecting
and preserving the meta-bodies.

00:04:39.990 --> 00:04:42.790
At last! At last, this day's come!

00:04:42.790 --> 00:04:43.860
Sis!

00:04:43.860 --> 00:04:44.620
May-yen!

00:04:47.130 --> 00:04:49.570
It's amazing! I can't believe it!

00:04:49.570 --> 00:04:53.170
Shizuno-sempai, we can be reborn now!

00:04:53.170 --> 00:04:53.970
Yeah.

00:04:53.970 --> 00:04:56.730
What's with that reaction?!
C'mon, be happier!

00:05:03.510 --> 00:05:06.810
Reborn... Into the real world...

00:05:09.050 --> 00:05:12.720
I... I'd rather... stay as I am.

00:05:14.460 --> 00:05:16.580
What... What did you just say?

00:05:18.130 --> 00:05:23.130
Wh-What's the point of regaining
our physical bodies now?

00:05:23.130 --> 00:05:25.640
I want to stay as I am.

00:05:25.640 --> 00:05:28.370
Kuroshio-sempai, what are you saying?!

00:05:28.370 --> 00:05:30.130
Be quiet, Kyo.

00:05:32.610 --> 00:05:37.910
Commander Shima...
You have no right to decide our fates.

00:05:38.450 --> 00:05:40.180
There's no time left.

00:05:40.180 --> 00:05:42.290
We have all the time in the world.

00:05:42.290 --> 00:05:45.490
Because we're meta-bodies
who never age or die.

00:05:45.490 --> 00:05:50.480
I'm sick of it! I'm tired of feeling like
you're manipulating me, Commander!

00:05:53.500 --> 00:05:54.830
Kuroshio...

00:05:55.200 --> 00:05:58.690
We must all be of
one mind about this...

00:06:06.480 --> 00:06:10.410
Still, I was really surprised.
Kuroshio just suddenly saying that...

00:06:10.810 --> 00:06:12.680
What's with him?

00:06:12.680 --> 00:06:14.450
The argument is sound.

00:06:15.590 --> 00:06:18.690
Even if we face the risk and become
flesh and blood humans again,

00:06:18.690 --> 00:06:20.890
we'll have a life span of,
at most, 60 more years.

00:06:20.890 --> 00:06:24.020
I wonder if people would
really be happy about that.

00:06:24.960 --> 00:06:26.190
Kaminagi...

00:06:27.560 --> 00:06:29.960
We rushed into this, didn't we?

00:06:30.470 --> 00:06:32.440
Kuroshio was correct.

00:06:32.440 --> 00:06:34.530
The only one who has no time is me.

00:06:36.940 --> 00:06:38.440
We could have dealt with this...

00:06:38.440 --> 00:06:41.340
if we still had the Maihama
server's regulation system.

00:06:41.740 --> 00:06:43.680
There's nothing left of it now.

00:06:43.950 --> 00:06:47.610
I see. So, that's where you
both kept disappearing to.

00:06:50.520 --> 00:06:52.450
What are you all doing here?

00:06:54.190 --> 00:06:57.190
Forgive me, Commander. But...

00:06:57.190 --> 00:07:00.290
But, I share the
same doubts as them!

00:07:01.030 --> 00:07:02.730
I see.

00:07:02.730 --> 00:07:05.270
What was this "regulation system"?

00:07:05.270 --> 00:07:09.340
Can I just say it was my family
doctor and leave it at that?

00:07:09.340 --> 00:07:11.070
I'm afraid not.

00:07:11.070 --> 00:07:13.980
I've thought it was all kinda
weird for a while now.

00:07:13.980 --> 00:07:17.850
The design and construction of
the Zegapain and our carriers...

00:07:17.850 --> 00:07:21.450
Even the establishment
of our current battle plans.

00:07:21.450 --> 00:07:23.450
I hear it's all your doing.

00:07:23.450 --> 00:07:24.750
And so?

00:07:24.750 --> 00:07:28.530
And then the fact that you moved
the Maihama server to the moon.

00:07:28.530 --> 00:07:33.220
I find it hard to believe a normal
Cerebrant could pull that off!

00:07:33.430 --> 00:07:36.490
So, tell us...
Just who the hell are you two?

00:07:41.640 --> 00:07:44.670
Not knowing that
won't impede this operation.

00:07:44.670 --> 00:07:45.980
Yes, it will!

00:07:45.980 --> 00:07:50.040
If we can't trust you, you'll have nobody
willing to carry out the final operation!

00:07:50.480 --> 00:07:56.510
And just how are we supposed
to trust you now, Commander?

00:07:58.520 --> 00:08:01.150
Then let's postpone the operation.

00:08:01.390 --> 00:08:02.520
Commander!

00:08:15.270 --> 00:08:17.010
Toga! Quit wasting your shots!

00:08:17.240 --> 00:08:19.040
You're consuming Q.L. too fast!

00:08:20.810 --> 00:08:23.210
So, we'll get a Q.L. charge, okay?!

00:08:23.210 --> 00:08:24.510
Fosetta!

00:08:24.510 --> 00:08:26.140
<i>Fast as ever, I see!</i>

00:08:27.980 --> 00:08:30.110
Here comes your Q.L.
Make sure you catch it!

00:08:35.290 --> 00:08:36.830
Q.L. charging, complete!

00:08:36.830 --> 00:08:37.850
Overflowing!

00:08:42.430 --> 00:08:45.630
Projected course for the Viagems
leads to the enemy Arctic core server!

00:08:45.940 --> 00:08:47.670
Toga! Shoot down at least one of those ships!

00:08:47.670 --> 00:08:50.240
Where's the fun in that?
I'm heading straight into them!

00:08:50.240 --> 00:08:51.800
Holo-Bolt Pressure!

00:08:52.040 --> 00:08:53.810
Caladrius, cover Toga!

00:08:53.810 --> 00:08:54.500
Roger!

00:08:57.010 --> 00:09:00.350
Data, Q.L. load.
Phalanx shot, physicalizing!

00:09:05.220 --> 00:09:07.190
EAT THIS!!!

00:09:15.670 --> 00:09:17.370
Mission complete.

00:09:17.370 --> 00:09:21.390
<i>Good job. Toga, Sarah, return to</i>
<i>the ship and take a nice, long rest.</i>

00:09:21.940 --> 00:09:24.470
I don't think we've <i>ever</i>
had a "nice, long rest."

00:09:24.470 --> 00:09:26.110
<i>Heh... I suppose not.</i>

00:09:26.110 --> 00:09:30.170
Hey, Isola?
Why exactly are we fighting like this?

00:09:30.410 --> 00:09:32.210
<i>It's never gonna end, is it?</i>

00:09:32.980 --> 00:09:34.880
For a shining future.

00:09:34.880 --> 00:09:36.990
<i>You really think we have one?</i>

00:09:36.990 --> 00:09:38.580
Of course we do.

00:09:38.820 --> 00:09:41.480
<i>Don't we, Shima?</i>

00:09:42.360 --> 00:09:43.620
Maybe...

00:09:45.260 --> 00:09:49.290
Maybe Kuroshio-sempai
thinks of you as being strange.

00:09:50.130 --> 00:09:52.930
He wonders why you
can accept it so genuinely.

00:09:55.740 --> 00:09:57.370
Well...

00:09:57.370 --> 00:10:00.010
The real world is full of hardship.

00:10:00.010 --> 00:10:01.740
No cities, no houses.

00:10:01.740 --> 00:10:03.510
No convenience stores, no cell phones...

00:10:03.880 --> 00:10:05.480
Hey, what are you saying?

00:10:05.480 --> 00:10:08.810
Are you saying we should do something
we want to while we still can?

00:10:15.890 --> 00:10:18.160
This is the best
you could come up with?

00:10:18.460 --> 00:10:23.170
Well, since we're here, let's eat up
all the specials, right, Kaminagi?

00:10:23.170 --> 00:10:25.730
I envy you. Your purity...

00:10:29.040 --> 00:10:31.700
Kuroshio-sempai. Irie-sempai.

00:10:32.080 --> 00:10:34.340
You guys out for a big, last meal, too?

00:10:34.340 --> 00:10:36.280
We always come here.

00:10:38.480 --> 00:10:40.350
You didn't like what
I said before, did you?

00:10:42.090 --> 00:10:45.710
I don't care what you think of me.
I have no intention of leaving here.

00:10:46.190 --> 00:10:50.220
Maybe things do gradually get a
little stale in this looping world, but...

00:10:51.960 --> 00:10:55.020
But... It's better than dying.

00:10:55.360 --> 00:10:58.700
Except, this place isn't all
eternal life and youth.

00:10:59.070 --> 00:11:00.660
Once the server reaches
the end of its life span...

00:11:01.000 --> 00:11:05.370
If we use the Zegas to constantly
do the external maintenance,

00:11:05.370 --> 00:11:07.310
we'll extend its life span.

00:11:07.780 --> 00:11:09.250
I suppose, but...

00:11:09.250 --> 00:11:11.810
But can you really call this "living?"

00:11:12.850 --> 00:11:15.480
I envy you. You're lucky.

00:11:16.090 --> 00:11:19.490
You forget about all the bad and
unpleasant things about the way things are.

00:11:19.820 --> 00:11:22.760
Maybe a guy like you can make
things work with Kaminagi.

00:11:22.860 --> 00:11:23.830
What?

00:11:23.990 --> 00:11:25.150
Stop.

00:11:25.700 --> 00:11:28.100
But the problem is,
we remember everything.

00:11:28.100 --> 00:11:30.100
That's why I don't want to die.

00:11:30.100 --> 00:11:33.800
Throwing our lives away in a worthless battle?

00:11:34.140 --> 00:11:36.240
I say to hell with it.

00:11:36.240 --> 00:11:37.540
Why, you!

00:11:39.610 --> 00:11:43.200
What do you mean, worthless?
What the hell do you know?!

00:11:43.450 --> 00:11:45.410
We're the ones doing the fighting!

00:11:45.410 --> 00:11:48.980
Don't cop an attitude when all
you do is sit on your ass all day!

00:11:49.990 --> 00:11:52.390
Let him go. We're sorry.

00:11:56.090 --> 00:11:58.820
You really have forgotten the
way things are, haven't you?

00:11:59.660 --> 00:12:02.260
Even though I got more kills than you have!

00:12:03.670 --> 00:12:06.030
We were both pilots, originally.

00:12:06.800 --> 00:12:07.930
Zegapain's.

00:12:18.850 --> 00:12:22.340
I ask this to you,
who has melted into all of us.

00:12:23.150 --> 00:12:25.750
Naga, what is life?

00:12:31.030 --> 00:12:34.360
We originally came from the Shizuoka server.

00:12:34.360 --> 00:12:36.230
We fought all over the world...

00:12:36.230 --> 00:12:38.700
and finally ended up
under Shima's command.

00:12:39.040 --> 00:12:41.170
We fought desperately, nearly dying.

00:12:41.170 --> 00:12:43.070
Day after day...

00:12:43.070 --> 00:12:45.410
Time after time,
wandering on the edge of death.

00:12:45.410 --> 00:12:46.710
Reborn, time after time...

00:12:46.940 --> 00:12:49.340
Reborn?! You guys, too?

00:12:49.710 --> 00:12:51.580
It's an ordinary thing in this world.

00:12:52.180 --> 00:12:56.740
Our bodies could no longer take
the stress of combat in the Zega.

00:12:57.190 --> 00:12:59.710
Still, I prefer living, even like this.

00:12:59.790 --> 00:13:02.720
All the Cerebrants from
the Shizuoka server were...

00:13:03.490 --> 00:13:04.530
That's why.

00:13:04.530 --> 00:13:07.190
I... I forgot all about that.

00:13:09.030 --> 00:13:11.800
Sogoru, you really do
trust them, don't you?

00:13:12.800 --> 00:13:15.670
Those two.
You don't find them strange?

00:13:15.970 --> 00:13:16.730
Well...

00:13:17.310 --> 00:13:22.010
Yeah, the president is kinda
suspicious, but Shizuno-sempai is...

00:13:22.010 --> 00:13:24.340
I just feel I can trust her.

00:13:24.680 --> 00:13:27.080
I see. Is that the power of love?

00:13:27.080 --> 00:13:30.080
Probably because your
previous version and her were...

00:13:33.060 --> 00:13:34.580
What should I do?

00:13:36.130 --> 00:13:39.530
Should I stay here?
Or should I go back to being human?

00:13:40.860 --> 00:13:43.800
I dunno. You're a special case.

00:13:43.800 --> 00:13:46.470
In the end, you won't be
happy in either world.

00:13:46.470 --> 00:13:47.830
Sempai!

00:13:50.570 --> 00:13:54.100
Kaminagi. Where are you going?!
Hey, Kaminagi!

00:13:57.250 --> 00:13:59.540
I'm a total jackass, aren't I?

00:13:59.920 --> 00:14:01.980
Yeah, you are.

00:14:10.460 --> 00:14:13.900
<i>I see.</i>
<i>So, Shima's made his decision, then?</i>

00:14:13.900 --> 00:14:18.960
Yes. That's why I'd like your
opinion on this, Commander Isola.

00:14:19.670 --> 00:14:21.270
<i>Why ask me?</i>

00:14:21.270 --> 00:14:23.640
Because I respect you.

00:14:24.170 --> 00:14:27.010
You did a lot for me in the past.

00:14:28.210 --> 00:14:30.770
<i>I treasure the memories of those days.</i>

00:14:39.960 --> 00:14:45.220
You two fought well back when the
Zegapain was our newest asset.

00:14:46.060 --> 00:14:48.590
You fought one hard battle after another.

00:14:49.470 --> 00:14:53.830
To be talking together like this...
I think it's almost a miracle.

00:14:54.500 --> 00:14:57.730
<i>That's why I want to go on living.</i>

00:14:58.980 --> 00:15:00.940
I understand your situation.

00:15:00.940 --> 00:15:04.170
However, until we're formally notified,
I'll pretend I didn't hear this.

00:15:05.850 --> 00:15:08.990
Should we be reborn
or remain as meta-bodies?

00:15:08.990 --> 00:15:11.290
Which will make us happier?

00:15:11.290 --> 00:15:13.290
What is "life"?

00:15:13.290 --> 00:15:15.690
I don't think you'll ever get an answer to that.

00:15:16.730 --> 00:15:19.020
Proceed as you think you should.

00:15:19.660 --> 00:15:23.930
<i>However, you have no right to interfere with</i>
<i>those who want to be resurrected, either.</i>

00:15:24.570 --> 00:15:26.660
<i>Don't forget that.</i>

00:15:27.600 --> 00:15:28.430
<i>Good night.</i>

00:15:32.610 --> 00:15:35.770
<i>I'll proceed, as I think I should.</i>

00:15:41.350 --> 00:15:44.320
What's wrong?
You look upset, Kaminagi.

00:15:46.820 --> 00:15:50.220
Kyo, do you still love Shizuno-sempai?

00:15:50.360 --> 00:15:52.380
Wha! What's brought that up?!

00:15:52.700 --> 00:15:54.100
Do you?

00:15:54.100 --> 00:15:55.290
Uh...

00:15:58.730 --> 00:16:00.790
Well, I don't hate her...

00:16:01.300 --> 00:16:03.860
Never mind. I'm fine.

00:16:04.270 --> 00:16:06.880
Kyo, don't worry about me so much.

00:16:06.880 --> 00:16:09.000
You should think about yourself more.

00:16:10.350 --> 00:16:12.280
Don't say that.

00:16:12.280 --> 00:16:14.270
That was just someone
who was kinda like me.

00:16:14.680 --> 00:16:16.620
He died and was reborn.

00:16:17.090 --> 00:16:20.280
So, you'll live like he did,
holding it in when you get hurt?

00:16:20.760 --> 00:16:24.660
I don't want that!
It isn't fair to you or to me!

00:16:24.990 --> 00:16:27.020
No, that's not what I meant!

00:16:27.430 --> 00:16:30.960
I don't want it to be my fault
that you aren't happy!

00:16:31.530 --> 00:16:33.970
You don't have to bear
every burden by yourself!

00:16:33.970 --> 00:16:36.570
All the hardships, all the sad things...

00:16:36.570 --> 00:16:38.870
Or else you'll end up
destroying yourself!

00:16:39.610 --> 00:16:40.870
Kaminagi...

00:16:47.050 --> 00:16:49.310
Maybe that was how the old me acted...

00:16:49.820 --> 00:16:51.720
I've been thinking about it lately.

00:16:51.720 --> 00:16:53.490
Because I wonder if
I'll get my memories back,

00:16:53.490 --> 00:16:56.660
and because of the weird way
everyone worries about me.

00:16:56.660 --> 00:16:59.220
I've been thinking about
a lot of stuff, too.

00:16:59.500 --> 00:17:03.800
Maybe we should try to think together.
You and me.

00:17:04.400 --> 00:17:08.060
It's like I said! If we do that,
you'll just end up destroying yourself!

00:17:09.940 --> 00:17:14.140
I'm a burden for you...
Way too big of a burden!

00:17:27.320 --> 00:17:28.650
Shima!

00:17:30.590 --> 00:17:32.390
I've decided, Yehl.

00:17:32.760 --> 00:17:36.160
I will continue to walk the path I believe in.

00:17:36.430 --> 00:17:39.400
Are you saying... Tell them everything?

00:17:40.140 --> 00:17:43.040
If it leads to agreement, then yes.

00:17:45.470 --> 00:17:48.380
The pain that leads to happiness, huh?

00:18:00.020 --> 00:18:02.620
As commander of the Oceanus,
I'm ordering you.

00:18:04.960 --> 00:18:07.900
We will proceed with the
final operation, as planned!

00:18:09.270 --> 00:18:10.400
Commander!

00:18:10.400 --> 00:18:13.700
There will be no change!
Resurrection will be our goal!

00:18:14.040 --> 00:18:17.900
W-Wait just a minute here!
What about Kaminagi?

00:18:18.170 --> 00:18:21.440
Can she be resurrected to
be the way she was before?!

00:18:21.440 --> 00:18:22.680
We'll work on it.

00:18:22.680 --> 00:18:24.010
Work on it?!

00:18:24.010 --> 00:18:25.240
Trust me!

00:18:26.820 --> 00:18:28.820
This is reckless.

00:18:28.820 --> 00:18:32.690
You're rushing the decision
before we've all agreed to it?

00:18:32.690 --> 00:18:35.250
How will going to the moon
allow us to be reborn?!

00:18:35.690 --> 00:18:38.630
You have to at least
explain that much to us!

00:18:39.860 --> 00:18:42.260
I recognize that you all
have many doubts about this.

00:18:42.830 --> 00:18:45.000
Once the operation
is successfully completed,

00:18:45.000 --> 00:18:48.700
I'll let every individual decide if
they wish to remain in the server.

00:18:49.240 --> 00:18:51.930
You'll be free to stay or free to leave.

00:18:53.010 --> 00:18:55.700
That's good enough for now,
isn't it, Kuroshio?

00:18:56.110 --> 00:18:59.010
No. I choose the third option.

00:19:01.320 --> 00:19:03.250
We surrender to the Gards-orm.

00:19:07.090 --> 00:19:08.720
Kuroshio-sempai!

00:19:08.720 --> 00:19:10.960
However, with two conditions.

00:19:10.960 --> 00:19:12.660
That they guarantee our lives...

00:19:12.660 --> 00:19:17.160
and that they use their technology
to resurrect us as Reconstructants!

00:19:24.470 --> 00:19:27.000
Abyss... He's late.

00:19:33.680 --> 00:19:35.510
Welcome back, Abyss!

00:19:37.120 --> 00:19:39.180
The mind unification is over.

00:19:39.720 --> 00:19:43.120
The lightless ones
have earned Naga's holy wrath.

00:19:47.360 --> 00:19:50.100
It's impossible!
Become Reconstructants?!

00:19:50.100 --> 00:19:52.470
Become like Abyss and Sin?!

00:19:53.000 --> 00:19:56.240
Exactly. They have physical bodies,

00:19:56.240 --> 00:19:59.500
but they can die and come back
to life over and over.

00:19:59.910 --> 00:20:04.400
That's truly mankind's ideal form.
Don't you think so?

00:20:06.150 --> 00:20:09.950
You gotta be kidding!
Those things aren't human!

00:20:09.950 --> 00:20:11.920
I've had enough of your surrender talk!

00:20:11.920 --> 00:20:14.120
Shut up. Just shut up!

00:20:14.860 --> 00:20:16.160
What was that?!

00:20:16.160 --> 00:20:18.290
You can't call the Reconstructants human.

00:20:18.990 --> 00:20:23.660
They're monsters, created by Naga's
warped ideas in the name of evolution.

00:20:24.230 --> 00:20:28.570
Those creatures have no
concept of peace or surrender.

00:20:28.840 --> 00:20:30.640
How can you be so sure?!

00:20:30.640 --> 00:20:33.010
What do you guys
know about the Gards-orm?!

00:20:33.280 --> 00:20:37.910
We know! At the very least,
more than you do! As for why...

00:20:53.660 --> 00:20:54.260
Shima!

00:20:54.260 --> 00:20:55.600
Mr. President!

00:20:55.600 --> 00:20:57.360
Commander Shima!

00:21:09.240 --> 00:21:12.880
With the creation of Sabato,
the lightless ones shall be exterminated.

00:21:12.880 --> 00:21:16.410
And then we shall redraw the
world according to our ideals!

00:21:17.090 --> 00:21:19.210
That is Naga's wish!

00:22:51.850 --> 00:22:54.780
Mission to resurrect mankind, commencing.

00:22:54.850 --> 00:23:00.160
It's finally begun. The final operation,
which has close to zero chance for success.

00:23:00.160 --> 00:23:03.150
It's not "close" to zero.
It <i>is</i> zero.

00:23:03.230 --> 00:23:09.060
I may not like it, but I think Shizuno-sempai
and Kyo should be together for this.

00:23:09.060 --> 00:23:10.630
Do you really think so?

00:23:10.630 --> 00:23:12.530
Yes, I do. I really do.

00:23:12.530 --> 00:23:15.700
Next, on Zegapain: "G-Phaetus."

00:23:15.700 --> 00:23:18.110
My pain, never to be forgotten.
